## SQ-LGM-07 | Omurice feast: 4 bowls then the plate; full and part-eaten drops (block at 200)
@group A
@commands `/setblock ~ ~ ~ largemeals:omurice_block`, bot right-clicks with bowls 5 times; break a full and a `[servings=2]` one
@pass 4 Bowl of Omurice, then the plate leftover; full drops the feast item, part-eaten a bowl (LGM-09, 10)
@fails FeastBlock property names
@from batches/r1102b/s3_A.qb
> setblock 200 -60 500 largemeals:omurice_block
> pbot spawn lg7 200 -60 503 minecraft:overworld survival
> pbot hold lg7 minecraft:bowl 5
repeat 5
> pbot use lg7 200 -60 500 up
end
> clear lg7 largemeals:omurice 0
> data get block 200 -60 500
expect Found 4 matching item
> setblock 200 -60 500 largemeals:omurice_block
> zact break 200 -60 500 none
> setblock 200 -60 500 largemeals:omurice_block[servings=2]
> zact break 200 -60 500 none
expect \[zact\] break 200 -60 500 largemeals:omurice_block held none: true, .*drops largemeals:omurice_block x1$
expect \[zact\] break 200 -60 500 largemeals:omurice_block held none: true, .*drops minecraft:bowl x1$
> pbot remove lg7
look after the 4th bowl the block is the plate leftover (5th use); the setblock state name servings fits FeastBlock

